	   ***  tAo v3.3 PARAMETERS FILE  ***
	       (default unities : I.S.)


This project intends to show the
evolution of the gravity anomalies
during foreland basin formation.

PARAMETER	CORRESPONDING 		USE
 VALUES		  VARIABLES
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Gridding:
201 		nx		Number of x points (distance).
201		nz		Number of z points (depth for rheological calculations).

Limits:
0		x0		Modelizated x range.
5e5		xf

Window:
140e3		xmin		Limits of the output window.
300e3		xmax
-14000		ymin
4000		ymax


Lithosph. geometry:
20000		espelastdefault	Default ET (if no .EET file) 
34000		espcortdefault	Default crustal geometry for gravity anomaly
15000		espcortsup 	 and rheological calculations when no .CRUST and .UCRUST
00		alt0 		Altitude of  the initial plate position from sea level.


Densities:
3300		densmanto	Mantle.
2800		denscort	Crust (just for anomaly calculation).
2800		densinfill	Infilling material (only when switch_topoest=1).
2300		denssedim	Sediments.
0		densamb		Air (or water for oceanic flexure), 


Erosion model parameters:
2e6		Kerosdif, 	Diffusive erosion constant.
.3		Keroseol, 	Continental background erosion rate constant.
200		Ksedim, 	Water sedimentation rate [m/Ma].



Time variables [Ma]:
0		Timeini		Initial time.
20		Timefinal	Final time.
5		tau		Relaxation time.
1		dt		Increment time.
5		dtmemounit	Time elapsed between units recording. 
				  if = 0 only file-defined load units will be recorded. 


Boundary Conditions:
2		boundary_conds	#0: Continuous simetric half-plate.
				#1: Broken plate (left).
				#2: Continuous plate.
				#3: Free ends.
				#4: Hunging plate.
				#5: Broken plate (right).

External forces:
0e12		tecforce	Horizontal tectonic force (compressive if >0).
0e12		appshearforce	Applied force as bound. cond. in case 1. (left side).
0e16		appmoment 	Torque as bound. cond. case 1. (left side).


0	switch_rheolimit & lith_type	
				#0: Pure elastic plate model
				#1: Pure elastic plate model
				#2: Elastic-plastic oceanic lithosphere.
				#3: Elastic-plastic continental always decoupled.
				#4: Elastic-plastic continental never decoupled.
				#5: Elastic-plastic continental auto. decoupling.


These are switches to turn on options of the model.
Their possible values are 1 (yes) or 0 (no):
1	switch_mar		For existence of sea.
1	switch_erosed		For erosional-deositional model.
1	switch_calcanom		For gravity anomaly calculation.

i/o switches:
1	switch_write_file	For file output.
1	switch_ps		For postscript output.
0	switch_output		For graphic output(PV-WAVE).
0	switch_verbose		For more runtime prints.
0	switch_debug		For more runtime prints.


